    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1059">

                <pb facs="1108" n="1098" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1098"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.1561/6–1649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-16T17:00:00+08:00">June 16, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 17—3:27 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 597. Tung Ling, Vice Foreign Minister, tells me Minister National
                        Defense<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1059-f1"/> has drawn up definite plan for
                    closure all ports in Communist hands and that in next day or two we would
                    receive formal notification from Chinese Government closure these ports. Action
                    would apply to aircraft as well as surface vessels.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1059-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 399, Shanghai 342.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1059-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1059-f1-content">
                <p>Marshal Yen Hsi-shan, President of the Chinese Executive Yuan (premier).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1059-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1059-f2-content">
                <p>For text of notification dated June 20, see telegram Cantel No. 638, June 23,
                        <ref target="#pg1103">p. 1103</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
